               "summary":  "Samsung Electronics rallied 8.11% to KRW 191,900 on November 24, 2026 after Nvidia reinstated CEO Jensen Huang on November 23, yet shares remain 48.8% below their June 52-week high of KRW 374,500. Fundamentally, Q3 2026 results on October 29 broke records with KRW 195.3 trillion in revenue and KRW 107.4 trillion in operating profit as HBM4 shipments scaled for Nvidia\u0027s Vera Rubin platform. However, November brought U.S. export pauses on 16nm China orders, a Goldman Sachs target cut to KRW 350,000 on November 23 over 2028 memory pricing, and bearish technicals.",
